    "show_share": true,
    "description": "For 60-year-old Haseeb Sarwar* vision problems were affecting his everyday life. Sarwar had already lost sight in his right eye to a mismanaged cataract and, more devastating, was fast losing vision in his left to a developing cataract. After doing the rounds of local ophthalmologists, he finally decided to make the seven-hour journey from Jacobabad to Karachi to visit doctors at the Aga Khan University Hospital.",
